 ('ferigo','Ferigo Fang','Master of the Dredger','a mud-spattered man sounding the channel with a marked pole',"“A hand shallower than last month,” he says. “Ferigo Fang. The lagoon is always trying to become a field.”","Ferigo says if he stopped for ten years the galleys would be rowing through grass.","“Doges come and go,” Ferigo says. “Mud stays. So do I.”",'deck','scow'),
