 ('sandro','Sandro Sepa','Cuttle-Catcher of the Flats','an old man with a lantern and a small three-pronged spear',"“Follow the sticks,” he says. “Sandro Sepa. I have walked here sixty years. The mud took my brother in the first.”","Sandro sells the ink to the scriveners and the rest to the cooks.","“The tide gives you two hours,” Sandro says. “It does not give three.”",'flats','markers'),
