 ('cecilia','Cecilia Merl','Lace-Maker of the Isle','a woman moving a dozen bobbins without seeming to choose among them',"“A thumb’s width a day,” she says. “Cecilia Merl. A collar is a season. A bride’s veil is a winter and my eyes.”","Cecilia says the pattern came from mending nets, and the nets are still better made.","“He knots to catch fish,” Cecilia says. “I knot to catch senators’ wives.”",'doorways','nets'),
